<!--Post: 2087--><!--Time: 1103309012-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2087"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Murco<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Murco<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 10:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->it&#39;s probable that he cut the phone <BR>lines, then posed as someone from the phone co. and asked <BR>them to check their phone for service...etc. he did have an id. <BR>what do you think?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2087-->
<!--Post: 2701--><!--Time: 1103956500-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2701"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Canada<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Canada<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 10:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sounds reasonable. The only thing I cannot figure out is why didn&#39;t someone notice a stranger lurking around cutting telephone lines in the first place? Does anyone live right next door to the victims or are the homes acres away from each other. I have always pictured a subdivision like scenario with close neighbors....am I wrong?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2701-->
<!--Post: 2703--><!--Time: 1103962546-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2703"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 12:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->All of the victims lived in houses with neighbors very close all around.  I agree that how he escaped notice, if he did, is one of the biggest questions.  I believe he either was or posed as some type of utility person.  Like a phone man.  Walk through the neighborhood wearing a set of coveralls and a tool belt, nobody would notice.  And your idea of cutting the phone likes and presenting himself as a repairman is a very good one.  I would  not be surpirsed if you were very close to the truth.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2703-->
<!--Post: 2715--><!--Time: 1104006335-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2715"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 12:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->We dont know if the lines were cut inside or outside do we&#62;? ...We also dont know if they were cut before or after he entered the premises...Before would allow him to pose as a repair man...if they were cut after it may have been to disallow the victims to call for help IF they were at all able to...just my thoughts<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2715-->
<!--Post: 2798--><!--Time: 1104155556-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2798"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 5:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Having lived in Wichita for 30 years, I&#39;m familiar with these neighborhoods.  These were small homes on small lots with neighbors within 30 or 40 feet.  Strangers would be noticed.  Also the Otero and Wegerle homes fronted onto highly traveled streets.  During the 70&#39;s, 80&#39;s, and 90&#39;s the east side of Wichita had no efficient arterial streets.  North/South travel used Woodlawn, Edgemoor, Oliver, and Hillside.  East/West used Lincoln, Kellogg, Douglas, Central, and 13th.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2798-->
<!--Post: 2963--><!--Time: 1104342100-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2963"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dawgar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dawgar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 9:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->January 1974 <BR> <BR> <BR>Victims&#39; children return home; clues sought <BR> <BR>BY THE WICHITA EAGLE <BR> <BR> <BR>Hannon said at the scene of the crime Tuesday that the mass slayings &#34;borders on a type of execution&#34; in that the telephone line leading into the home had been cut. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2963-->
